What is Router-on-a-Stick?

A method where one physical router interface uses multiple subinterfaces to route between VLANs.

Project 1 - Router-on-a-Stick Office Network

Technologies:
- Cisco Packet Tracer/GNS3
- VLANs
- Trunking
- Inter-VLAN Routing
- Router-on-a-Stick

Skills Demonstrated:
- Network Segmentation
- Layer 2 Switching
- Layer 3 Routing
- Troubleshooting



Lab Topology
                 Router R1
                  e0/0
                    |
              Trunk Link
                    |
                  SW1 e0/3
    e0/0    ------------------------
        |          |e0/1          |e0/2
 e0     PC1        PC2 e0        PC3 e0
